        "original_id": "4c8640b7-6344-5a4c-93ba-d3da8c39745c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Rousillon Rupes, Titania\n- Systems: Voyager 2\n- People: William Shakespeare, Bertram count of Rousillon\n- Products: All's Well That Ends Well, First Folio\n\nFacts:\n- All's Well That Ends Well is a play by William Shakespeare that is believed to have been written between 1604 and 1605.\n- All's Well That Ends Well was originally published in the First Folio in 1623.\n- Voyager 2 first imaged Rousillon Rupes in January 1986.\n- Rousillon Rupes is a scarp on the surface of Titania.\n- Rousillon Rupes was named after Bertram, count of Rousillon, from William Shakespeare's comedy All's Well That Ends Well.\n- The term rupes is Latin for cliff, and Rousillon reflects an Elizabethan English misspelling of Roussillon.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
